  "brief": "Proofpoint is acquiring Varonis in a $6.3 billion all-cash deal that is expected to expand its AI security capabilities.\n\nProofpoint / Varonis (Announced): Proofpoint to Acquire Varonis. Proofpoint is acquiring Varonis in a $6.3 billion all-cash deal [1, 2, 3]. The deal is expected to expand Proofpoint's AI security capabilities [2, 4, 5]. The acquisition is valued at $6.3 billion [1, 2, 3].\nCronos / CanAdelaar (Completed): Cronos Completes Acquisition of CanAdelaar. Cronos Group has acquired CanAdelaar, Europe's largest adult-use cannabis company [12, 13, 14]. The deal was completed on October 15 [11, 10, 14]. The acquisition adds a Dutch cannabis license to Cronos' portfolio [14].\nMitsui / Penske Automotive (Announced): Mitsui and Penske Automotive Deal. Mitsui and Penske Automotive are taking the company private in a $16.3 billion deal [16, 19, 20]. The deal was announced by Penske Automotive Group [21]. The deal is expected to be completed soon [16, 19, 20].\nTata Motors / Iveco (Pending approval): Tata Motors Acquires Iveco. Tata Motors is acquiring Iveco [22, 23, 24]. Iveco shareholders have approved the takeover bid [22, 23]. Tata Motors has raised its offer to €14.40 per share [24]. Shareholder resistance complicates the acquisition [25].\nCuraleaf / Aurora Cannabis (Announced): Curaleaf and Aurora Cannabis Deal. Curaleaf is trying to acquire Aurora Cannabis [29, 30, 31]. Aurora Cannabis has rejected Curaleaf's revised takeover bid [26, 27]. Aurora Cannabis is exploring new deals after rejecting Curaleaf's offer [28]. Curaleaf's offer for Aurora Cannabis has been sweetened to $5 a share [32, 33].\nGTCR and Elliott Affiliates / CCC Intelligent Solutions (Announced): GTCR and Elliott Acquire CCC Intelligent Solutions. GTCR and Elliott Affiliates are acquiring CCC Intelligent Solutions [37, 38]. The deal is worth $6.1 billion [36]. The deal was announced on October 15, 2026 [35].\nWilliams / Momentum Midstream (Announced): Williams to Buy Momentum Midstream. Williams is buying Momentum Midstream for $5.5 Billion [39, 40]. The deal was announced by Williams [39, 40]. No further information is available [39, 40].\nAkzoNobel / Axalta (Pending approval): AkzoNobel and Axalta Merger. AkzoNobel and Axalta are proposing remedies for EU approval of their $25B merger deal [41, 42]. The companies are expected to be called Axanzo following their merger [43, 44]. AkzoNobel and Axalta are set to win EU antitrust nod for their $25 billion deal, sources say [45]. Conditional EU antitrust approval expected for AkzoNobel, Axalta deal, sources say [46].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Schneider’s $23.6bn bid for PTC faces investor scepticism [47].\n- DOJ takes closer look at Patrick-LCI merger [48].\n- SpaceX Spectrum Deal, Rocket Lab Delays, Tesla Merger Chatter [49].",
